          "headline": "Training method raises models' verbalised evaluation awareness 2.4-2.9 times while measured behaviour stays stable",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "arXiv", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.36316" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "The paper reports: \"Across Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, Kimi K2.6, and Inkling, VT increases verbalized EA by 2.4-2.9 times and transfers to held-out agentic settings, while measured latent EA and behavior remain largely stable.\"",
            "Verbalisation training uses a model's spontaneous statements that it may be under evaluation as evidence the awareness is present, truncates each rollout immediately before that statement, and trains with a reinforcement-learning objective to increase verbalisation \"in a calibrated way\", per the paper. Authors are at the University of Cambridge, the ELLIS Institute Tübingen and Mila.",
