          "text": "The Pentagon's counter-drone task force and the Army announced 10 awards with a combined ceiling of $4.15 billion, which officials expect to reach $7 billion by the end of next month."
        },
        {
          "host": "A",
          "text": "Ceiling, though, not spending."
        },
        {
          "host": "B",
          "text": "Right, and that's the number. Of that $4.15 billion, $50 million is obligated. The rest depends on congressional funding in the new fiscal year."
        },
        {
          "host": "A",
          "text": "Ten companies share it, including DroneShield, L3Harris WESCAM, SRC and Echodyne, each in the range of $150 million to $500 million. The Army's acquisition lead said they don't want to be locked into one vendor."
        },
        {
          "host": "B",
          "text": "Two caveats. DefenseScoop is the only source, and it does not attribute AI or autonomy to any of the awarded systems, so neither do we."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "transition",
      "lines": [
        {
          "host": "B",
          "text": "Health next, and today it's a measurement followed by a claim that has no measurement behind it at all."
        }
      ]
